ntion to detail or memory for numbers, and how it might affect operational safety. According to system instruction, we must answer using explicit facts from our notes, meeting discussion, and tool answers. We have notes: Candidate B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills. Also we have from James: \"relatively weak memory for numbers\". Also from Emily: \"relatively weak memory for numbers\". So we have that observation. We need to discuss how that might affect operational safety. We can note that weak memory for numbers could impact tasks like fuel calculations, navigation entries, checklists, etc., potentially increasing risk of errors. However we must not infer beyond the given facts. We can say that a weak memory for numbers may pose a risk in tasks requiring precise numerical data, which are safety-critical. We can note that while B is conscientious, this specific weakness could affect attention to detail. Provide balanced view.\n\nWe must not include metadata, just answer."}
